<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title><%= portalName %> Portal — ST. JOSEPH'S CHANDEL</title>
<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.6.0/css/all.min.css">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>body{background:#0f1115;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;}</style>
</head>
<body class="text-[#f5f6f8] flex items-center justify-center min-h-screen px-4">
  <div class="text-center max-w-sm">
    <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-5 mx-auto" style="background:#22262e"><i class="fa-solid fa-hammer text-2xl" style="color:#8B5CF6"></i></div>
    <h1 class="text-lg font-extrabold mb-2">Hi <%= user.name %> 👋</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#9aa1ac] leading-relaxed mb-6">The <%= portalName %> web portal is being built next. For now the Admin portal is fully wired up to the database — the <%= portalName.toLowerCase() %> mobile app already covers this role.</p>
    <form method="POST" action="/logout"><button class="font-bold py-3 px-6 rounded-2xl text-white" style="background:#8B5CF6">Back to Login</button></form>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
